    "faqs": [
      {
        "q": "How can I apply for AU Vetta Credit Card?",
        "a": "You can apply for AU Small Finance Bank Vetta Credit Card online via official website of AU Small Finance Bank. The application process involves filling out a form, submitting necessary KYC documents, and completing identity verification."
      },
      {
        "q": "How can I earn reward points with AU Vetta Credit Card?",
        "a": "You can earn 4 reward points per Rs. 100 on grocery and departmental store purchases, 2 reward points per Rs. 100 on other retail spends and 1 reward point per Rs. 100 spent on utility & telecom categories."
      },
      {
        "q": "What are the milestone benefits associated with AU Vetta Credit Card?",
        "a": "AU Vetta Credit Card offers milestone rewards to encourage regular usage. Cardholders can earn 500 bonus points on spending Rs. 50,000 per quarter, an additional 1,000 bonus points for spending Rs. 1 Lakh per quarter, and Rs. 1,000 worth of vouchers on annual spends of Rs. 2.5 Lakh."
      },
      {
        "q": "Does AU Vetta Credit Card offer lounge access?",
        "a": "Yes, the card offers complimentary domestic & international lounge visits. You get 1 complimentary domestic lounge visit per quarter, 2 complimentary railway lounge visits per quarter, and 1 international lounge visit per quarter through the Priority Pass program."
      },
      {
        "q": "Is there a fuel surcharge waiver with this card?",
        "a": "Yes, the card offers a 1% fuel surcharge waiver on fuel transactions ranging between Rs. 400 and Rs. 5,000. The waiver is capped at Rs. 250 per statement cycle, making it a useful benefit for regular fuel spenders."
      },
      {
        "q": "How can I redeem reward points earned via AU Vetta Credit Card?",
        "a": "Reward points earned on AU Vetta Credit Card can be redeemed through the AU 0101 app or the net banking portal. The points can be used to avail e-gift vouchers, merchandise, or other redemption options offered by the bank, depending on the number of points accumulated."
      }
    ]
  },
